From 0faa81a84d877412266005d17f6ff639c2b0db76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:19:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] perf(sim): B2 G2 bound the cold services pieces: a cell
 floor, smaller tier steps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dense1m from load still had services steps of 3-5 ms in the first passes:
the once-per-pass cell loops (corridor, hashes, the provider sum, the road
count, the stop cells and compose, the access seeds, the access / shop
rows, the combos, the stale records, NIMBY's corridors, the tier clamp and
stats rows) ran at ~0.1 µs per cell, 25-70 x their warm cost, and a tier
step of 0.3 ms of units took 2-4.4 ms.

- params.ts INFRA_CELL_SIZING_US = 0.004: a piece of such a loop holds at
  most pieceUnits(INFRA_CELL_SIZING_US, 1, budget) cells (~16k at half
  INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS). Chunk sizes only: the estimates keep the loops'
  own coefficients.
- The tier steps' budget is half INFRA_PIECE_MS; a final row item (a
  slot's clamp or stats) runs alone in its step, at most the floor's rows.
- The stop disks use a quarter of INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS; the police need's
  monthly scan coefficient doubles (0.03 -> 0.06 µs per building).

Only step boundaries move (b2PiecesServices: every pass end equal at
every piece size). catchments.test 'perf: 256²' compares the cached and
fresh passes on the tier steps, where the reach cache acts (design §10
G2): the whole pass also holds the fixed costs and the states the cache
does not touch, and its second pass is the NIMBY one (ratio 0.62 < 0.75,
tier steps 0.41 < 0.6).

